WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.910
Be found on Google, get reviews, and track what really sells.

2
00:00:04.260 --> 00:00:09.040
This is the video for module two: search, local visibility and analytics.

3
00:00:10.290 --> 00:00:16.630
A customer who searches is already looking for what you sell. That is the warmest customer you can get.

4
00:00:16.980 --> 00:00:24.150
Google does not search the whole internet at that moment. Its programs follow links and discover pages in advance.

5
00:00:25.400 --> 00:00:29.940
Google stores what each page is about in a giant library called the index.

6
00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:37.800
When someone searches, it ranks the most relevant and useful pages, and checks how well they work on a phone.

7
00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:47.050
Cake is impossible to win. Birthday cake delivery Ikeja is realistic, because big brands do not compete hard for it.

8
00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:55.190
Ronke bakes cakes at home in Ikeja. She typed birthday cake into Google and noted the suggestions under the box.

9
00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:01.200
She added her area: birthday cake delivery Ikeja, custom cakes Ikeja.

10
00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:08.100
She asked five customers. Two said cake vendor in Ikeja, a phrase she had not thought of.

11
00:01:09.350 --> 00:01:11.810
She chose one main phrase for each page.

12
00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:26.030
She used it in the page title and first paragraph, naturally. Stuffing a phrase into every sentence reads badly and does not help. And be wary of anyone who promises number one on Google in a week.

13
00:01:27.280 --> 00:01:38.930
When someone searches hair salon Surulere, Google often shows a map with three businesses first. Those come from Google Business Profile. Use your name exactly as it is on your signboard.

14
00:01:40.180 --> 00:01:43.800
Choose the most accurate category, such as Bakery or Tailor.

15
00:01:45.050 --> 00:01:49.190
If you work from home, hide your address and set a service area instead.

16
00:01:50.440 --> 00:01:57.030
Verify the profile, then fill in everything. Wrong hours are one of the quickest ways to lose trust.

17
00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:04.810
Google ranks local results by relevance, distance and prominence. Reviews build prominence and trust.

18
00:02:06.060 --> 00:02:16.110
Halima runs a salon in Kano. She sent her review link to 48 happy clients. About 1 in 4 left a review, taking her from 4 to 16.

19
00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:26.140
One client gave 2 stars after waiting 40 minutes. Halima thanked her, apologised, and explained that she now confirms times the evening before.

20
00:02:27.390 --> 00:02:34.930
Never fake, buy or pay for reviews. Google's rules forbid it, and it can remove reviews or restrict your profile.

21
00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:47.720
With Google Ads you usually pay only when someone clicks. Quality matters too, so a relevant ad can beat a bigger bid. Ronke tests a campaign. These figures are illustrative.

22
00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:54.360
She sets about 5,000 naira a day for 20 days, which is 100,000 naira.

23
00:02:55.610 --> 00:03:09.100
At about 125 naira a click, that buys 800 clicks. Her page turns 3% into orders, so 24 orders. That is about 4,167 naira per order.

24
00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:23.420
Her profit per cake is about 9,000, so the campaign pays. But at 1%, each order would cost 12,500, more than her profit. The landing page matters as much as the ad.

25
00:03:24.670 --> 00:03:34.340
Google does not call or WhatsApp you demanding payment. Pay only inside your own account at ads dot google dot com, and never share your codes.

26
00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:47.980
Ngozi sells skincare and added UTM labels to her Easter links, so Google Analytics could see where each visitor came from. Instagram brought 600 visits and 12 purchases.

27
00:03:49.230 --> 00:03:55.820
WhatsApp brought only 150 visits, but 9 purchases. That is 6%, three times better.

28
00:03:57.070 --> 00:04:06.210
Email converted at 4%. So she grows her WhatsApp list, with permission, and keeps Instagram for awareness. Watch orders, not likes.

29
00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:17.380
No website? Ask every new customer, how did you hear about us, and record it. Each Monday, fill in one row for last week, and write one decision to test.

30
00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:22.030
Keep the sheet private, because names and phone numbers are personal data.

31
00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:30.750
To remember. Use the local phrases your customers type. Complete your Google profile, and ask honestly for reviews.

32
00:04:31.100 --> 00:04:36.840
Keep cost per order below your profit per sale. And measure messages and orders, not likes.

33
00:04:38.090 --> 00:04:48.140
Now practise. Build a keyword list, complete your Google Business Profile and send five review links, plan a small campaign on paper, and start your weekly sheet.

34
00:04:48.490 --> 00:04:50.430
Continue with the lessons below.
